ers/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1793980320000-orchestrator-handoff-yang-clojure-seat-to-zcode.md), and the relevant sections of [publish.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc).\nI will now read the relevant sections of [clojure.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc) and [macro.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc).\nI will read the remaining lines of [clojure.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc) and [macro.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc).\nI will now read the beginning of [clojure.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc) where `annotate-call-sites` and the C1 validators are defined, and inspect recent git history and `collab/yang-clojure/` files.\nI will check the format of a prior architect findings log (`1794252349000-architect-cc1-crosshost-publication-regression-argon.gemini-4-argon-high.stdout.log`) and inspect the other files touched by cc1 (`b1b9abae`, `83b52a0b`, `b0463cd2`, `cd050ca2`).\nI will now read the remaining files modified by `cc1` and referenced in the design's A2 inventory: [prelude.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc), [call.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc), [uast.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc), [frontends.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc), and [encoder.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc).\nI will now read the relevant sections of [vm.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc), [linearize.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc), [derive.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc), and [safepoint.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc).\nI will now read [ast_walker.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc), [semantic.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc), [ast_index.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/ast_index.cljc), [stage.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/stage.cljc), [module.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/module.cljc), and [publication.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/publication.cljc).\nI will now search the codebase for references to `call-site`, `annotate-call-sites`, `slice9_site_tables`, and related symbols, and read the relevant sections of [repl.cljc](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc), [latte_oracle_test.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj), [latte_oracle_tables.clj](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj), and [attribution_inventory.md](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md).\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-10 12:58:26 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-10 19:58:26 +07\n\n# Lead System Architect Scoping: `yang.clojure` Adoption Rounds 2–4 + `D1` (Post-`cc1`)\n\n**Evaluated against**: `master` at `8cd9fc92` (`origin/master` when prompt was authored: `8dbe7031`; delta `8dbe7031..8cd9fc92` is collab docs/merge `d4a4fc8e` from `feat/p5b2-lifecycle` only).\n\n---\n\n## 1. What Round 1 (`cc1`) Delivered vs. Design §3.2 and §5.3\n\n### 1.1 Covered by `cc1` (`b1b9abae` + follow-ups `cd050ca2`, `83b52a0b`, `b0463cd2`)\n\n1. **Frontend map-AST C1 marker & coverage validator (`src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc`, `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc`)**:\n   - [`annotate-call-sites`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/uast.cljc#L129-L151) walks `vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar` child slots and attaches `:yang/call-site 1` to every `:application` map node without touching non-application nodes.\n   - [`application-occurrences`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc#L1612-L1623) derives all `[root path]` pairs from [`occurrences`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc#L1589-L1609) whose node type is `:application`.\n   - [`yang.clojure`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L62-L265) defines `call-site-key` (`:yang/call-site`), `call-site-version` (`1`), `*call-site-finalizing*` ([`yang/clojure.cljc:72-76`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L72-L76)), [`eligible-application-sites`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L93-L100), [`call-site-metadata`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L103-L115) (sorted deterministically with `jing/canonical-compare`), [`marked-application-sites`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L118-L127), [`validate-call-site-coverage!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L140-L250) (supporting transport-deduped mode, `:declared? true`, and `:per-occurrence-origins? true` with multi-claim refusal `:yang/call-site-multi-claim` at [`yang/clojure.cljc:210-216`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L210-L216)), and [`validate-ast-call-sites!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L253-L264).\n   - Every public Clojure compilation entry point finalizes its returned map AST with `annotate-call-sites`:\n     - [`compile-form`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2249-L2262) (via `*call-site-finalizing*` outer guard) and [`compile`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3068-L3091).\n     - [`compile-program`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2392-L2625) (annotated at [`:2459`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2459) on both `:native` and `:arg-vector`/`:outcomes` paths, including when `:bundle-prelude? true` bundles `yang.core.call/uast` and `yang.clojure.prelude/uast`).\n     - [`lower-unit`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3224-L3255) (re-annotated at [`:3255`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3255) after [`publish-to-globals`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3171-L3221) rewrites top-level definitions/reads into `clj/define-global!` and `clj/global-get` applications).\n   - Published Clojure runtime modules and donor kits are C1-finalized:\n     - [`yang.clojure.prelude/module-uast`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc#L108-L112) (`clj` module).\n     - [`yang.core.call/module-uast`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc#L168-L175) (`yang.call` module). *(Note: [`yang.core.call/uast`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc#L158-L165) itself is not wrapped in `u/annotate-call-sites`; Clojure's `compile-program` annotates the whole combined tree at `:2459`, whereas non-Clojure callers of `call/uast` receive unannotated AST until their own seats adopt C1.)*\n     - Exception-kit Clojure donor publications finalized in `b0463cd2` ([`test/yang/call/conformance.clj:99-106`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/conformance.clj#L99-L106), [`test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj:79-85`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/exception_legs.clj#L79-L85), [`test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj:81-87`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/call/exception_probes.clj#L81-L87)).\n   - REPL frontend catalog manifest updated in [`yin.repl.frontends/clojure-manifest`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/frontends.cljc#L42-L60) (`:yang.frontend/revision \"c1-1\"`, `:yang.frontend/support-profile :yang.clojure/c1`).\n\n2. **Encoder boundary enforcement & per-member claim propagation (`src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc`)**:\n   - [`marked-call-sites`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L237-L261) and [`check-call-site-claim!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L264-L294) validate every member's C1 claim before stripping `:yang/call-site` from canonical AST rows.\n   - [`program-batch`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L297-L345) emits `frontend-metadata` (`[[[:yang/call-site 1] #{[root path] ...}] ...]`) and appends the 6th slot `call-site-claims` (`[bool ...]`) to `[:yin.program/batch ...]` when any member claims C1.\n\n3. **Macro expansion provenance, packet lineage, and post-expansion C1 finalization (`src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc`)**:\n   - Implements Owner Ruling U1–U3 ([`1795310000000-owner-ruling-occurrence-identity-unitarity.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1795310000000-owner-ruling-occurrence-identity-unitarity.md#L1-L33)): threads construction-time `::origin-of` metadata ([`yin/vm/macro.cljc:609-624`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L609-L624)), strips tracking metadata before `:data`/`:key` hashing ([`strip-tracking`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L635-L659)), preserves packet decomposition/reassembly lineage ([`register-lineage!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L670-L681), [`lineage-origin-for`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L684-L714), single choke point [`recover-rebuilt-packet`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L903-L907)), records 12-slot [`event-row`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1290-L1304) with [`output-correspondence`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1366-L1389), validates post-expansion C1 coverage in [`expand-batch`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1630-L1745) with [`final-call-site-metadata`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1598-L1627), and retains side tables on the expander consumer keyed by `[admission-origin final-root]` ([`call-site-table`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1842-L1856), [`load`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1859-L1882)).\n\n4. **Module publication & side-table custody (`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`)**:\n   - [`publish-closure!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L242-L386) enforces C1 coverage on `:clojure` modules, mints scoped admission tokens ([`admission-scope`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L123-L136), [`publication-origin`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L164-L177)), keeps `:yin.module/call-sites` out of the schema-1 hashed manifest (`83b52a0b`, [`publish.cljc:345-378`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L345-L378)), materializes the side-table entity and `:yang.call-site/schema 1` record naming `:yang.call-site/manifest`, and exposes [`published-call-site-table`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L434-L480).\n\n5. **Focused test suite (`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`)**:\n   - 14 `deftest`s ([`clojure_callsite_test.cljc:99-1238`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc#L99-L1238)) pinning static coverage, boundary validation, macro provenance, twin identical content, encoder per-member claims, packet reassembly provenance, and publisher scope admission identity.\n\n### 1.2 What `cc1` Did NOT Cover (Remaining from Design §3.2 and §5.3)\n\n| Design Surface ([`1794670000000`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md)) | Current State on `master` (`8cd9fc92`) | Exact File & Line Citations |\n|---|---|---|\n| **§3.2 Row 5 / §2.4**: Projected `{:root :rows}` member in `encoder/project-member` | Drops `:frontend-metadata` unconditionally (`:frontend-metadata []`) when caller passes an already-projected `{:root :rows}` map. | [`src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc:108-114`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L108-L114) |\n| **§3.2 Row 7 / §2.4**: `yang.safepoint/derive-envelope` | Emits `:yin/frontend-metadata []` on derived tree `A'` and does not recompute C1 on `A'` or emit an input-to-output occurrence correspondence for injected `(check-safepoint)` applications. | [`src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc:234-256`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc#L234-L256) |\n| **§3.2 Row 12 & REPL session index-to-module bridge**: `yin.vm.linker.publish/module-from-index` and `yin.repl` | 1. [`indexed-programs`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L487-L501) reconstructs map ASTs from `$code` datoms via `vm/datoms->ast` (which carries no `:yang/call-site` keys), and [`sequenced`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L527-L541) synthesizes unmarked `:application` nodes; [`module-from-index`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L562-L635) returns `{:yin.module/language :Index ...}` with unannotated ASTs and ignores the session's `(:call-site-tables (:expander state))`.<br>2. [`yin.repl/render-compile-output`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc#L1808-L1822) discards `:call-sites` from `macro/expand-batch`, and [`yin.repl`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc#L1205-L1231) never exposes or persists `macro/call-site-table`. | [`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:487-635`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L487-L635), [`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1205-1231`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc#L1205-L1231), [`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1808-1822`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc#L1808-L1822) |\n| **§3.2 Rows 8–9 / §2.5**: Lowering provenance (`linearize`, `derive/stack-image`, `derive/register-image`, `publish-closure!`) | 1. [`linearize/project-rows`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L188-L214) emits `:provenance` (`[pc [root-address path]]`, without `origin`), which [`publish-closure!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L312) and [`yin.repl/packet->vector`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc#L156-L158) immediately discard by selecting `(:vector ...)`.<br>2. [`linearize/project-datoms`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L283-L302) emits `[pc entity-id]` with no bridge to `[origin root-address path]`.<br>3. [`derive/stack-image`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L103-L119) and [`derive/register-image`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L168-L184) emit no call-instruction provenance table `[segment-address pc origin root-address path]`. | [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc:188-214`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L188-L214), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc:283-302`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L283-L302), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc:103-184`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L103-L184), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:312`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L312) |\n| **§3.2 Rows 10–11 / §2.5**: Runtime caller-`K` propagation & trace emission across evaluators | None of the evaluators ([`ast_walker.cljc:273-332`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc#L273-L332), [`semantic.cljc:142-276`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc#L142-L276), `stack.cljc`, `register.cljc`) propagate caller occurrence key `K = [origin root-address path]` or emit `[callee-identity selected-arity caller-K]` traces. The LaTTe oracle still uses its harness-local `kernel-stamp-sites` integer counter + `gate-site-slot` cell (instantiation #1, [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1983-2321`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L1983-L2321)). | [`src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:273-332`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc#L273-L332), [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:142-276`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc#L142-L276), [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1983-2321`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L1983-L2321) |\n| **§5.1, §5.2, §5.3**: Four-host Clojure acceptance & cross-host occurrence-key replay equality gate | `clojure_callsite_test.cljc` has been verified on JVM and compiled on Dart (`cd050ca2`), and `83b52a0b` restored `yang.core.call-test` cross-host manifest hash parity, but there is no four-host (JVM, Node, Dart, Jolt) replay equality test asserting byte-identical `[origin root-address path]` C1 side tables across hosts, nor a Jolt load/parity gate run for `clojure_callsite_test`. | [`collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:207-237`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L207-L237), [`collab/yang-call/1795010000000-orchestrator-reply-equality-gate-per-frontend.md:1-13`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-call/1795010000000-orchestrator-reply-equality-gate-per-frontend.md#L1-L13) |\n| **§4, §6, §7, §8**: `D1` durable correspondence record, independent reconstruction verifier, and static/dynamic budget gates | `slice9_site_tables.edn` is still at `:version 1` keyed by harness-sequential integer site IDs (`1..N`) rather than C1 occurrence keys `K = [origin root-address path]`; no `:yang.correspondence/schema 1` or `:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema 1` exists yet. | [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn:1-2`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn#L1-L2), [`src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj:1-65`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj#L1-L65), [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3284-3293`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3284-L3293) |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Decomposition of Adoption Rounds 2–4: Handoff Conflict & Recommended Scoping\n\n### 2.1 Explicit Conflict Between the Outgoing Handoff and the Design of Record\n\nThe outgoing orchestrator handoff ([`collab/yang-clojure/1794400000000-orchestrator-handoff-yang-clojure-seat-final.md:19,87`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794400000000-orchestrator-handoff-yang-clojure-seat-final.md#L19)) states:\n> *\"Adoption rounds extend the C1 call-site attribution across the remaining yang.clojure surfaces (the three-kind correspondence: ambient literals, context-API carriers, delegation exclusion). Round 1 shipped with cc1; rounds 2–4 remain.\"*\n\n**This reading conflicts with the signed rulings and the codebase on `master`:**\n1. **The \"three-kind correspondence\" is LaTTe-oracle consumer logic, NOT a `yang.clojure` compiler surface, and it is ALREADY landed on `master`.**\n   - In commit `d794382e` (merged via `a7dc47c2` and audited in `0f04212b`), [`kernel-ambient-correspondence`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L1863-L1980) and [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md:31-53`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md#L31-L53) already implement all three correspondence kinds (`:ambient-delegation` with `:ambient-literal`, `:context-shift` for context-API carriers, and `:context-copy`) plus `:delegation?` exclusion ([`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2077-2114`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L2077-L2114)).\n   - Design §2.2 ([`1794670000000:54-57`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L54-L57)) and Addendum A v3 ([`1794630000000:13-22`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794630000000-architect-attribution-addendum-a-RECORD.md#L13-L22)) explicitly forbid putting ambient-literal, context-carrier, or delegation semantics into `yang.clojure` or C1:\n     > *\"It carries no language name, source arity, ambient-context classification, or callee identity. Those are consumer evidence derived by the oracle or another explicitly versioned consumer.\"*\n2. **Where the number \"rounds 1–4\" actually came from in the Design:**\n   - In Design §5.3 ([`1794670000000:227-237`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L227-L237)), the four frontend adoption steps are the **four languages** (1. Clojure first, 2. Python, 3. TypeScript, 4. PHP), while across the Clojure/pipeline track itself, the remaining post-`cc1` work before `D1` is the **three-stage pipeline progression** in Design §2.4–§2.5, §3.2, §5.1–§5.2, and §6–§7:\n     - Stage A (Round 2): Pipeline & transform C1 preservation (`safepoint`, `encoder/project-member`, `repl`/`module-from-index`).\n     - Stage B (Round 3): Lowering provenance & runtime/oracle C1 occurrence-key (`K = [origin root-address path]`) integration.\n     - Stage C (Round 4): Four-host Clojure C1 replay equality gate (JVM, Node, Dart, Jolt) + §6 static/dynamic budget verification.\n\n**Question for Owner Ruling**:\n- *Should Rounds 2–4 on the `yang.clojure` seat be scoped as the three remaining Clojure/pipeline stages required by Design §2.4–§2.5, §3.2, §5.1–§5.3, and §6 (recommended below), OR if \"Rounds 2–4\" was only shorthand for the 4-frontend sequence (where 2–4 belong to Python/TS/PHP seats), should `yang.clojure` collapse the remaining Clojure-side prerequisites into a single pre-`D1` round and proceed directly to `D1`?*\n\n### 2.2 Recommended Decomposition of Clojure Adoption Rounds 2–4\n\nAssuming the three-round Clojure-track decomposition prior to `D1`:\n\n#### Round 2 (`cc2`): Transform & Session C1 Preservation (`safepoint`, `encoder`, `module-from-index`, `yin.repl`)\n- **Goal**: Close the remaining static/transform C1 holes in Design §2.4 and §3.2 (Rows 5, 7, 12) so no Clojure compilation, safepoint rewrite, or REPL index-publication path silently strips C1 claims.\n- **Files to touch**:\n  - [`src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc#L234-L256): In `derive-envelope`, when the input tree or envelope carries C1 metadata (or when requested for a C1-claiming frontend), recompute `:yin/frontend-metadata` on derived tree `A'` (`(check-safepoint)` synthetic `:application` nodes get C1 markers) and attach an explicit `:yang.safepoint/correspondence` map linking surviving pre-safepoint application occurrences to their `A'` paths and marking injected `(check-safepoint)` occurrences as `:safepoint/injected` (Design §2.4, [`1794670000000:86`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L86)).\n  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L108-L114): In `project-member`, preserve an explicit `:frontend-metadata` key on an already-projected `{:root :rows}` member instead of hardcoding `:frontend-metadata []`, and validate it when `:call-site-claim?` is true.\n  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L487-L635) and [`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc#L1205-L1231): Thread the expander's retained `(:call-site-tables (:expander state))` (or optional `:call-site-tables` option in `module-from-index`) and annotate synthesized sequence wrapper applications in [`sequenced`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L527-L541) when publishing a C1-claimed session module; surface `:call-sites` in [`render-compile-output`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc#L1808-L1822) when non-empty.\n  - [`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc): Add unit tests for `safepoint/derive-envelope` C1 preservation + injected-site correspondence, pre-projected `{:root :rows}` encoder members, and `module-from-index` C1 preservation.\n- **Prelude impact**: None (`src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc` untouched).\n- **Acceptance test**: Focused JVM/Node/Dart tests in `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` and `test/yang/safepoint_test.clj`.\n\n#### Round 3 (`cc3`): Lowering Provenance & Oracle C1 Occurrence-Key (`K = [origin root-address path]`) Bridge\n- **Goal**: Bridge the gap between `cc1`'s static/post-expansion occurrence keys `K = [origin root-address path]` and the LaTTe oracle's site-table attribution (Design §2.5, §3.2 Rows 8–10, §4.2), replacing or binding the harness-only sequential integer site IDs (`1..N`) to canonical C1 occurrence keys `K`.\n- **Architectural note on §2.5 vs. `D1`**:\n  - Currently, `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` ([`:1983-2114`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L1983-L2114)) stamps sequential integer site IDs (`1..N`) into guest source *before* `yang/compile-program` runs (`kernel-stamp-sites`), and executes on `:walker` and `:semantic` using a guest cell `gate-site-slot`.\n  - Meanwhile, [`linearize/project-rows`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L188-L214) already computes `:provenance` (`[pc [root-address path]]`) on the expanded canonical tree `A`.\n  - To satisfy Design §2.5 and prepare `D1` (§4.2) without breaking the 4,000,000-instruction budget:\n    1. Extend [`yin.vm.semantic.linearize`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L188-L214) (and `derive/stack-image`, `derive/register-image` at [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc:103-184`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L103-L184)) to emit canonical call-instruction provenance `[segment-address pc origin root-address path]` when given an expanded packet + C1 side table (and retain it as an optional side artifact in [`publish-closure!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L312) outside the schema-1 manifest hash).\n    2. In [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L2077-L2164), compile each fixture's C program through the C1-enabled pipeline (`encoder/program-batch` -> `macro/expand-batch` with admission origin `[:oracle/fixture fixture-id]`), extract the post-expansion C1 occurrence keys `K = [origin root-address path]`, and bind each oracle site entry in `:site-table` to its exact C1 occurrence key `K` (verifying 1-to-1 bijection between stamped guest call sites and post-expansion C1 guest-call occurrences, and verifying that both `:walker` and `:semantic` lanes resolve each executed call to the identical `K`).\n- **Files to touch**:\n  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L188-L302)\n  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L60-L184)\n  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L305-L385)\n  - [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L1983-L2321)\n  - [`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc)\n- **Prelude impact**: None (`src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc` untouched).\n- **Acceptance test**:\n  - `clojure_callsite_test` verifies that every `:call` instruction PC in semantic, stack, and register images maps back to the exact C1 occurrence key `K = [origin root-address path]`.\n  - `latte_oracle_test` (`test-attribution-battery`, `test-kernel-differential-gate`) passes with every site entry carrying and verifying its canonical C1 occurrence key `K`.\n\n#### Round 4 (`cc4`): Four-Host Clojure C1 Replay Equality Gate & Budget Verification (Design §5.1, §5.2, §5.3, §6)\n- **Goal**: Complete the per-frontend cross-host acceptance gate mandated by Design §5.1–§5.3 ([`1794670000000:207-237`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L207-L237)) and the orchestrator relay ([`collab/yang-call/1795010000000-orchestrator-reply-equality-gate-per-frontend.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-call/1795010000000-orchestrator-reply-equality-gate-per-frontend.md#L1-L13)) across all four hosts (**JVM, Node, Dart, Jolt**), plus the static/dynamic budget verification (Design §6).\n- **Files to touch**:\n  - [`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc#L99-L131): Strengthen `equality-gate-test` with pinned expected canonical digests (`dao.jing` root addresses + sorted C1 `[origin root-address path]` vectors + published `clj` and `yang.call` side-table addresses) so running the suite on JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt proves cross-host bit-identical replay rather than single-host self-equality alone.\n  - [`src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj) (if needed to include `yang.clojure-callsite-test` in the Jolt verification lane, per [`collab/jolt/1794900000000-orchestrator-handoff-jolt-seat.md:33`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1794900000000-orchestrator-handoff-jolt-seat.md#L33)).\n- **Prelude impact**: None (`src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc` untouched).\n- **Acceptance test**:\n  - `yang.clojure-callsite-test` and `yang.core.call-test` green on JVM, Node (`shadow-cljs`), Dart (`cljd`), and Jolt.\n  - Measured static overhead (`<= 1.25x` row count / `<= 1.35x` CBOR bytes on `clj` and `yang.call` modules) and dynamic overhead (`<= 4,000,000` steps per fixture, `<= 1,000,000` trace records) recorded in the round findings (Design §6.1–§6.2, [`1794670000000:241-265`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L241-L265)).\n\n---\n\n## 3. What `D1` Requires (`:yang.correspondence/schema 1`)\n\nPer Design §4 ([`1794670000000:141-203`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L141-L203)):\n\n1. **Current State of `slice9_site_tables.edn` and `latte_oracle_tables.clj` on `master`**:\n   - [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn#L1-L2) is generated by [`write-kernel-gate-evidence!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3284-L3293) and standalone generator [`src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj#L1-L65).\n   - Its current top-level shape is:\n     ```clojure\n     {:version 1\n      :fixtures {fixture-id {:canonical-source-hash \"<sha256>\"\n                             :site-table {1 {:site 1 :callee '... :arg-shapes [...] :def '... :delegation? bool} ...}}}}\n     ```\n   - [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3412-L3415) only asserts `(= 1 (:version tables))` and fixture count equality in `test-kernel-gate-evidence-writer-round-trip`.\n\n2. **Exact Schema & Content Required for `D1`**:\n   - **Record schema (`:yang.correspondence/schema 1`)** (Design §4.2, [`1794670000000:155-177`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L155-L177)):\n     ```clojure\n     {:yang.correspondence/schema 1\n      :yang.correspondence/upstream-revision \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"\n      :yang.correspondence/compiler-revision {:git-sha \"<commit>\" :source-sha256 \"<sha256>\"}\n      :yang.correspondence/adaptation-version {:context 2 :kernel-assembly 4}\n      :yang.correspondence/rule-version 1\n      :yang.correspondence/recipe <canonical-address-of-DerivationRecipe>\n      :yang.correspondence/correspondences [<CanonicalCorrespondenceEntry> ...]\n      :yang.correspondence/fixtures\n      {fixture-id\n       {:canonical-source-hash \"<sha256>\"\n        :program-root <canonical-root-address>\n        :site-table {K {:occurrence K\n                        :site <int> ;; retained for additive compatibility with version 1 queries\n                        :callee <symbol-or-:dynamic>\n                        :arg-shapes [<ArgShape> ...]\n                        :def <symbol-or-nil>\n                        :delegation? <boolean>}}\n        :trace-digests {:c-walker <canonical-address>\n                        :c-semantic <canonical-address>}\n        :stale-sites [<site-or-K> ...]}}}\n     ```\n     where every `K` is a persisted C1 occurrence key `[origin root-address path]`.\n   - **Derivation recipe (`:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema 1`)** (Design §4.3, [`1794670000000:179-192`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L179-L192)):\n     - Pure data specification containing `:upstream-source-digest`, `:context-layer-digest`, `:adapter-rules-digest`, `:frontend-id` (`[:yang.frontend/clojure \"c1-1\"]`), `:macro-store-digest`, and `:lowering-options`, content-addressed via `dao.jing`.\n\n3. **Files `D1` Touches**:\n   - [`src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj#L1-L65): Extend to emit the `D1` correspondence record and recipe, and provide the standalone independent reconstruction verifier `verify-correspondence-record!`.\n   - [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3268-L3419): Update `kernel-compile`, `kernel-row`, `write-kernel-gate-evidence!`, and `test-kernel-gate-evidence-writer-round-trip` to emit and validate `:yang.correspondence/schema 1` (either upgrading `slice9_site_tables.edn` additively or writing `slice9_correspondence.edn` alongside `slice9_site_tables.edn` so existing `:version 1` readers never break).\n   - [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn) (and/or `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn`) + [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn).\n\n4. **Independent Reconstruction Procedure (Design §4.4, [`1794670000000:194-203`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L194-L203))**:\n   A standalone test/verifier function that takes the persisted `:yang.correspondence/schema 1` record and independently executes the 7 steps:\n   1. Verify `:upstream-revision`, `:compiler-revision`, and `:recipe` digests against the checkout.\n   2. Re-derive `correspondences` from pinned upstream forms + checked-in context layer and assert `=` with `:yang.correspondence/correspondences`.\n   3. Re-compile and macro-expand each fixture's C program under `:recipe` and assert `=` with `:canonical-source-hash` and `:program-root`.\n   4. Re-compute the C1 occurrence set `{[origin root-address path]}` and assert exact key equality with `(keys :site-table)`.\n   5. Re-derive `:callee`, `:arg-shapes`, `:def`, and `:delegation?` at each `K` from the expanded AST node at `path` under `root-address` and assert `=` with `:site-table`.\n   6. Verify `:c-walker` and `:c-semantic` trace digests and assert `:stale-sites` is `[]` for every passing fixture.\n   7. Re-run the attribution query over `(correspondences, site-table, traces)` and assert the credited `[symbol arity]` set matches `slice9_evidence.edn` (`165/165` admitted arities).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Prerequisites from the Design (§5.3, §8) vs. `master` Git History\n\n1. **Cell-ref authenticity sweeps**: **LANDED on `master`**.\n   - Clojure runtime/compiler cell-ref authenticity landed in `0b74b4bb`, `7a4b5fc9`, `bfe9a8d9` (merged via `ae91bb8d`).\n   - TypeScript `cell/authentic?` sweep landed in `1636e3e9` (merged via `3e3e1342`).\n   - PHP preludesites swept in-lane (`1ef2a18b`).\n   - Python 12 `py/cell?` sites relayed in `f7d88058` (tracked on the Python seat's authentic-sweep branch; does not block Clojure rounds).\n2. **J2 load-path fix & J2 re-run**: **Code fix LANDED (`e858a7cf`); Jolt-side load re-run was still marked pending at Jolt handoff (`1794900000000`)**.\n   - The `yang.clojure` Jolt reader-conditional fix landed in `e858a7cf` (`fix(yang.clojure): select the tools.reader require away under jolt`), and the CLJS/Dart reader-conditional follow-up landed in `16a20a24`.\n   - Per [`collab/jolt/1794900000000-orchestrator-handoff-jolt-seat.md:34`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1794900000000-orchestrator-handoff-jolt-seat.md#L34), the Jolt seat noted: *\"The J2 load check for a6c25106e ... has not been done. A single jolt-lane load of yang.clojure on current master satisfies it.\"* This can be executed directly as part of Round 4 (`cc4`) Jolt parity verification.\n3. **Attribution-as-query & H3-6 independent audit**: **LANDED and PASSED on `master`**.\n   - Inventory landed in `30b2f610` ([`test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md)).\n   - Implementation landed in `d794382e` (merged in `a7dc47c2`).\n   - H3-6 independent audit findings P1/P2 were fixed and verified PASSED in `0f04212b`.\n4. **Inventory refresh (`attribution_inventory.md`)**: **PARTIALLY STALE against `master`**.\n   - [`test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md#L1-L267) was written in `30b2f610`/`d794382e` *before* `cc1` (`b1b9abae`) and `0f04212b` landed, so its line citations into `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` and `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` are shifted.\n5. **Stale Citations in Design (`1794670000000`) Against Current `master` (`8cd9fc92`)**:\n   - **`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`**: Design cites `compile-form` (`:2044`), `compile-program` (`:2186`), `compile` (`:2861`), `lower-unit` (`:3017`). On `master` (`8cd9fc92`, after `cc1` inserted 205 lines at `:62-265`), these are at [`compile-form` (`:2249`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2249), [`compile-program` (`:2392`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2392), [`compile` (`:3068`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3068), and [`lower-unit` (`:3224`)](file:///Users/st