{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/yang-clojure/1794314809000-architect-adoption-rounds-2-4-d1-scoping-r2.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md | sed -n '80,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"    80\t   - In Design §5.3 ([`1794670000000:227-237`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L227-L237)), the four frontend adoption steps are the **four languages** (1. Clojure first, 2. Python, 3. TypeScript, 4. PHP), while across the Clojure/pipeline track itself, the remaining post-`cc1` work before `D1` is the **three-stage pipeline progression** in Design §2.4–§2.5, §3.2, §5.1–§5.2, and §6–§7:\n    81\t     - Stage A (Round 2): Pipeline & transform C1 preservation (`safepoint`, `encoder/project-member`, `repl`/`module-from-index`).\n    82\t     - Stage B (Round 3): Lowering provenance & runtime/oracle C1 occurrence-key (`K = [origin root-address path]`) integration.\n    83\t     - Stage C (Round 4): Four-host Clojure C1 replay equality gate (JVM, Node, Dart, Jolt) + §6 static/dynamic budget verification.\n    84\t\n    85\t**Question for Owner Ruling**:\n    86\t- *Should Rounds 2–4 on the `yang.clojure` seat be scoped as the three remaining Clojure/pipeline stages required by Design §2.4–§2.5, §3.2, §5.1–§5.3, and §6 (recommended below), OR if \"Rounds 2–4\" was only shorthand for the 4-frontend sequence (where 2–4 belong to Python/TS/PHP seats), should `yang.clojure` collapse the remaining Clojure-side prerequisites into a single pre-`D1` round and proceed directly to `D1`?*\n    87\t\n    88\t### 2.2 Recommended Decomposition of Clojure Adoption Rounds 2–4\n    89\t\n    90\tAssuming the three-round Clojure-track decomposition prior to `D1`:\n    91\t\n    92\t#### Round 2 (`cc2`): Transform & Session C1 Preservation (`safepoint`, `encoder`, `module-from-index`, `yin.repl`)\n    93\t- **Goal**: Close the remaining static/transform C1 holes in Design §2.4 and §3.2 (Rows 5, 7, 12) so no Clojure compilation, safepoint rewrite, or REPL index-publication path silently strips C1 claims.\n    94\t- **Files to touch**:\n    95\t  - [`src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc#L234-L256): In `derive-envelope`, when the input tree or envelope carries C1 metadata (or when requested for a C1-claiming frontend), recompute `:yin/frontend-metadata` on derived tree `A'` (`(check-safepoint)` synthetic `:application` nodes get C1 markers) and attach an explicit `:yang.safepoint/correspondence` map linking surviving pre-safepoint application occurrences to their `A'` paths and marking injected `(check-safepoint)` occurrences as `:safepoint/injected` (Design §2.4, [`1794670000000:86`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L86)).\n    96\t  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L108-L114): In `project-member`, preserve an explicit `:frontend-metadata` key on an already-projected `{:root :rows}` member instead of hardcoding `:frontend-metadata []`, and validate it when `:call-site-claim?` is true.\n    97\t  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L487-L635) and [`src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc#L1205-L1231): Thread the expander's retained `(:call-site-tables (:expander state))` (or optional `:call-site-tables` option in `module-from-index`) and annotate synthesized sequence wrapper applications in [`sequenced`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L527-L541) when publishing a C1-claimed session module; surface `:call-sites` in [`render-compile-output`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc#L1808-L1822) when non-empty.\n    98\t  - [`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc): Add unit tests for `safepoint/derive-envelope` C1 preservation + injected-site correspondence, pre-projected `{:root :rows}` encoder members, and `module-from-index` C1 preservation.\n    99\t- **Prelude impact**: None (`src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc` untouched).\n   100\t- **Acceptance test**: Focused JVM/Node/Dart tests in `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc` and `test/yang/safepoint_test.clj`.\n   101\t\n   102\t#### Round 3 (`cc3`): Lowering Provenance & Oracle C1 Occurrence-Key (`K = [origin root-address path]`) Bridge\n   103\t- **Goal**: Bridge the gap between `cc1`'s static/post-expansion occurrence keys `K = [origin root-address path]` and the LaTTe oracle's site-table attribution (Design §2.5, §3.2 Rows 8–10, §4.2), replacing or binding the harness-only sequential integer site IDs (`1..N`) to canonical C1 occurrence keys `K`.\n   104\t- **Architectural note on §2.5 vs. `D1`**:\n   105\t  - Currently, `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` ([`:1983-2114`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L1983-L2114)) stamps sequential integer site IDs (`1..N`) into guest source *before* `yang/compile-program` runs (`kernel-stamp-sites`), and executes on `:walker` and `:semantic` using a guest cell `gate-site-slot`.\n   106\t  - Meanwhile, [`linearize/project-rows`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L188-L214) already computes `:provenance` (`[pc [root-address path]]`) on the expanded canonical tree `A`.\n   107\t  - To satisfy Design §2.5 and prepare `D1` (§4.2) without breaking the 4,000,000-instruction budget:\n   108\t    1. Extend [`yin.vm.semantic.linearize`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L188-L214) (and `derive/stack-image`, `derive/register-image` at [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc:103-184`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L103-L184)) to emit canonical call-instruction provenance `[segment-address pc origin root-address path]` when given an expanded packet + C1 side table (and retain it as an optional side artifact in [`publish-closure!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L312) outside the schema-1 manifest hash).\n   109\t    2. In [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L2077-L2164), compile each fixture's C program through the C1-enabled pipeline (`encoder/program-batch` -> `macro/expand-batch` with admission origin `[:oracle/fixture fixture-id]`), extract the post-expansion C1 occurrence keys `K = [origin root-address path]`, and bind each oracle site entry in `:site-table` to its exact C1 occurrence key `K` (verifying 1-to-1 bijection between stamped guest call sites and post-expansion C1 guest-call occurrences, and verifying that both `:walker` and `:semantic` lanes resolve each executed call to the identical `K`).\n   110\t- **Files to touch**:\n   111\t  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc#L188-L302)\n   112\t  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc#L60-L184)\n   113\t  - [`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L305-L385)\n   114\t  - [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L1983-L2321)\n   115\t  - [`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc)\n   116\t- **Prelude impact**: None (`src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc` untouched).\n   117\t- **Acceptance test**:\n   118\t  - `clojure_callsite_test` verifies that every `:call` instruction PC in semantic, stack, and register images maps back to the exact C1 occurrence key `K = [origin root-address path]`.\n   119\t  - `latte_oracle_test` (`test-attribution-battery`, `test-kernel-differential-gate`) passes with every site entry carrying and verifying its canonical C1 occurrence key `K`.\n   120\t\n   121\t#### Round 4 (`cc4`): Four-Host Clojure C1 Replay Equality Gate & Budget Verification (Design §5.1, §5.2, §5.3, §6)\n   122\t- **Goal**: Complete the per-frontend cross-host acceptance gate mandated by Design §5.1–§5.3 ([`1794670000000:207-237`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L207-L237)) and the orchestrator relay ([`collab/yang-call/1795010000000-orchestrator-reply-equality-gate-per-frontend.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-call/1795010000000-orchestrator-reply-equality-gate-per-frontend.md#L1-L13)) across all four hosts (**JVM, Node, Dart, Jolt**), plus the static/dynamic budget verification (Design §6).\n   123\t- **Files to touch**:\n   124\t  - [`test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc#L99-L131): Strengthen `equality-gate-test` with pinned expected canonical digests (`dao.jing` root addresses + sorted C1 `[origin root-address path]` vectors + published `clj` and `yang.call` side-table addresses) so running the suite on JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt proves cross-host bit-identical replay rather than single-host self-equality alone.\n   125\t  - [`src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj) (if needed to include `yang.clojure-callsite-test` in the Jolt verification lane, per [`collab/jolt/1794900000000-orchestrator-handoff-jolt-seat.md:33`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1794900000000-orchestrator-handoff-jolt-seat.md#L33)).\n   126\t- **Prelude impact**: None (`src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc` untouched).\n   127\t- **Acceptance test**:\n   128\t  - `yang.clojure-callsite-test` and `yang.core.call-test` green on JVM, Node (`shadow-cljs`), Dart (`cljd`), and Jolt.\n   129\t  - Measured static overhead (`<= 1.25x` row count / `<= 1.35x` CBOR bytes on `clj` and `yang.call` modules) and dynamic overhead (`<= 4,000,000` steps per fixture, `<= 1,000,000` trace records) recorded in the round findings (Design §6.1–§6.2, [`1794670000000:241-265`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L241-L265)).\n   130\t\n   131\t---\n   132\t\n   133\t## 3. What `D1` Requires (`:yang.correspondence/schema 1`)\n   134\t\n   135\tPer Design §4 ([`1794670000000:141-203`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L141-L203)):\n   136\t\n   137\t1. **Current State of `slice9_site_tables.edn` and `latte_oracle_tables.clj` on `master`**:\n   138\t   - [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn#L1-L2) is generated by [`write-kernel-gate-evidence!`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3284-L3293) and standalone generator [`src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj#L1-L65).\n   139\t   - Its current top-level shape is:\n   140\t     ```clojure\n   141\t     {:version 1\n   142\t      :fixtures {fixture-id {:canonical-source-hash \"<sha256>\"\n   143\t                             :site-table {1 {:site 1 :callee '... :arg-shapes [...] :def '... :delegation? bool} ...}}}}\n   144\t     ```\n   145\t   - [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3412-L3415) only asserts `(= 1 (:version tables))` and fixture count equality in `test-kernel-gate-evidence-writer-round-trip`.\n   146\t\n   147\t2. **Exact Schema & Content Required for `D1`**:\n   148\t   - **Record schema (`:yang.correspondence/schema 1`)** (Design §4.2, [`1794670000000:155-177`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L155-L177)):\n   149\t     ```clojure\n   150\t     {:yang.correspondence/schema 1\n   151\t      :yang.correspondence/upstream-revision \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"\n   152\t      :yang.correspondence/compiler-revision {:git-sha \"<commit>\" :source-sha256 \"<sha256>\"}\n   153\t      :yang.correspondence/adaptation-version {:context 2 :kernel-assembly 4}\n   154\t      :yang.correspondence/rule-version 1\n   155\t      :yang.correspondence/recipe <canonical-address-of-DerivationRecipe>\n   156\t      :yang.correspondence/correspondences [<CanonicalCorrespondenceEntry> ...]\n   157\t      :yang.correspondence/fixtures\n   158\t      {fixture-id\n   159\t       {:canonical-source-hash \"<sha256>\"\n   160\t        :program-root <canonical-root-address>\n   161\t        :site-table {K {:occurrence K\n   162\t                        :site <int> ;; retained for additive compatibility with version 1 queries\n   163\t                        :callee <symbol-or-:dynamic>\n   164\t                        :arg-shapes [<ArgShape> ...]\n   165\t                        :def <symbol-or-nil>\n   166\t                        :delegation? <boolean>}}\n   167\t        :trace-digests {:c-walker <canonical-address>\n   168\t                        :c-semantic <canonical-address>}\n   169\t        :stale-sites [<site-or-K> ...]}}}\n   170\t     ```\n   171\t     where every `K` is a persisted C1 occurrence key `[origin root-address path]`.\n   172\t   - **Derivation recipe (`:yang.correspondence.recipe/schema 1`)** (Design §4.3, [`1794670000000:179-192`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L179-L192)):\n   173\t     - Pure data specification containing `:upstream-source-digest`, `:context-layer-digest`, `:adapter-rules-digest`, `:frontend-id` (`[:yang.frontend/clojure \"c1-1\"]`), `:macro-store-digest`, and `:lowering-options`, content-addressed via `dao.jing`.\n   174\t\n   175\t3. **Files `D1` Touches**:\n   176\t   - [`src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj#L1-L65): Extend to emit the `D1` correspondence record and recipe, and provide the standalone independent reconstruction verifier `verify-correspondence-record!`.\n   177\t   - [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3268-L3419): Update `kernel-compile`, `kernel-row`, `write-kernel-gate-evidence!`, and `test-kernel-gate-evidence-writer-round-trip` to emit and validate `:yang.correspondence/schema 1` (either upgrading `slice9_site_tables.edn` additively or writing `slice9_correspondence.edn` alongside `slice9_site_tables.edn` so existing `:version 1` readers never break).\n   178\t   - [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn) (and/or `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn`) + [`test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn).\n   179\t\n   180\t4. **Independent Reconstruction Procedure (Design §4.4, [`1794670000000:194-203`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md#L194-L203))**:\n   181\t   A standalone test/verifier function that takes the persisted `:yang.correspondence/schema 1` record and independently executes the 7 steps:\n   182\t   1. Verify `:upstream-revision`, `:compiler-revision`, and `:recipe` digests against the checkout.\n   183\t   2. Re-derive `correspondences` from pinned upstream forms + checked-in context layer and assert `=` with `:yang.correspondence/correspondences`.\n   184\t   3. Re-compile and macro-expand each fixture's C program under `:recipe` and assert `=` with `:canonical-source-hash` and `:program-root`.\n   185\t   4. Re-compute the C1 occurrence set `{[origin root-address path]}` and assert exact key equality with `(keys :site-table)`.\n   186\t   5. Re-derive `:callee`, `:arg-shapes`, `:def`, and `:delegation?` at each `K` from the expanded AST node at `path` under `root-address` and assert `=` with `:site-table`.\n   187\t   6. Verify `:c-walker` and `:c-semantic` trace digests and assert `:stale-sites` is `[]` for every passing fixture.\n   188\t   7. Re-run the attribution query over `(correspondences, site-table, traces)` and assert the credited `[symbol arity]` set matches `slice9_evidence.edn` (`165/165` admitted arities).\n   189\t\n   190\t---\n   191\t\n   192\t## 4. Prerequisites from the Design (§5.3, §8) vs. `master` Git History\n   193\t\n   194\t1. **Cell-ref authenticity sweeps**: **LANDED on `master`**.\n   195\t   - Clojure runtime/compiler cell-ref authenticity landed in `0b74b4bb`, `7a4b5fc9`, `bfe9a8d9` (merged via `ae91bb8d`).\n   196\t   - TypeScript `cell/authentic?` sweep landed in `1636e3e9` (merged via `3e3e1342`).\n   197\t   - PHP preludesites swept in-lane (`1ef2a18b`).\n   198\t   - Python 12 `py/cell?` sites relayed in `f7d88058` (tracked on the Python seat's authentic-sweep branch; does not block Clojure rounds).\n   199\t2. **J2 load-path fix & J2 re-run**: **Code fix LANDED (`e858a7cf`); Jolt-side load re-run was still marked pending at Jolt handoff (`1794900000000`)**.\n   200\t   - The `yang.clojure` Jolt reader-conditional fix landed in `e858a7cf` (`fix(yang.clojure): select the tools.reader require away under jolt`), and the CLJS/Dart reader-conditional follow-up landed in `16a20a24`.\n   201\t   - Per [`collab/jolt/1794900000000-orchestrator-handoff-jolt-seat.md:34`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/jolt/1794900000000-orchestrator-handoff-jolt-seat.md#L34), the Jolt seat noted: *\"The J2 load check for a6c25106e ... has not been done. A single jolt-lane load of yang.clojure on current master satisfies it.\"* This can be executed directly as part of Round 4 (`cc4`) Jolt parity verification.\n   202\t3. **Attribution-as-query & H3-6 independent audit**: **LANDED and PASSED on `master`**.\n   203\t   - Inventory landed in `30b2f610` ([`test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md)).\n   204\t   - Implementation landed in `d794382e` (merged in `a7dc47c2`).\n   205\t   - H3-6 independent audit findings P1/P2 were fixed and verified PASSED in `0f04212b`.\n   206\t4. **Inventory refresh (`attribution_inventory.md`)**: **PARTIALLY STALE against `master`**.\n   207\t   - [`test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle/attribution_inventory.md#L1-L267) was written in `30b2f610`/`d794382e` *before* `cc1` (`b1b9abae`) and `0f04212b` landed, so its line citations into `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj` and `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` are shifted.\n   208\t5. **Stale Citations in Design (`1794670000000`) Against Current `master` (`8cd9fc92`)**:\n   209\t   - **`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`**: Design cites `compile-form` (`:2044`), `compile-program` (`:2186`), `compile` (`:2861`), `lower-unit` (`:3017`). On `master` (`8cd9fc92`, after `cc1` inserted 205 lines at `:62-265`), these are at [`compile-form` (`:2249`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2249), [`compile-program` (`:2392`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L2392), [`compile` (`:3068`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3068), and [`lower-unit` (`:3224`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc#L3224).\n   210\t   - **`src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc`**: Design cites `occurrences` at `:1589-1609`; `cc1` added [`application-occurrences`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc#L1612-L1623) immediately below it.\n   211\t   - **`src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc`**: Design cites `:232-279`; on `master` after `cc1`, C1 validation and `program-batch` are at [`:237-345`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc#L237-L345).\n   212\t   - **`src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc`**: Design cites `expand-all` (`:786-862`), `event-row` (`:1012-1025`), `expand-batch` (`:1303-1380`), `step`/`load` (`:1453-1556`). On `master` after `cc1`, these are at [`expand-all` (`:1060-1156`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1060-L1156), [`event-row` (`:1290-1304`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1290-L1304), [`expand-batch` (`:1630-1745`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1630-L1745), and [`step`/`call-site-table`/`load` (`:1818-1882`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc#L1818-L1882).\n   213\t   - **`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`**: Design cites `publish-closure!` (`:123-214`) and `module-from-index` (`:282-391`). On `master` after `cc1` and `83b52a0b`, `publish-closure!` is at [`:242-386`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L242-L386), `published-call-site-table` is at [`:434-480`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L434-L480), and `module-from-index` is at [`:562-635`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc#L562-L635).\n   214\t   - **`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`**: Design cites `kernel-stamp-sites` (`:1945-2040`), `kernel-site-table` (`:2043-2104`), `kernel-compile` (`:2112-2126`), `kernel-c` (`:2220-2283`), `write-kernel-gate-evidence!` (`:3230-3265`). On `master` after `0f04212b`, these are at [`kernel-stamp-sites` (`:1983-2074`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L1983-L2074), [`kernel-site-table` (`:2077-2141`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L2077-L2141), [`kernel-compile` (`:2149-2164`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L2149-L2164), [`kernel-c` (`:2257-2321`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L2257-L2321), and [`write-kernel-gate-evidence!` (`:3268-3303`)](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3268-L3303).\n   215\t   - **Design §3.1 (`:yin.module/call-sites` in `yin.module/schema 1` manifest)**: Superseded by `83b52a0b` (confirmed in [`1794252349000-architect-cc1-crosshost-publication-regression-argon.gemini-4-argon-high.stdout.log`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794252349000-architect-cc1-crosshost-publication-regression-argon.gemini-4-argon-high.stdout.log)), which excluded `:yin.module/call-sites` from the hashed `:yin.module/schema 1` manifest and linked the side table to the manifest via `:yang.call-site/manifest` instead.\n   216\t\n   217\t---\n   218\t\n   219\t## 5. Ordering, Dependency Graph, and Cross-Seat Collision Check\n   220\t\n   221\t```\n   222\t[cc1 (LANDED: b1b9abae, cd050ca2, 83b52a0b, b0463cd2)]\n   223\t        │\n   224\t        ├──► Round 2 (cc2): Transform & Session C1 Preservation\n   225\t        │      (safepoint.cljc, encoder.cljc:111, publish.cljc:module-from-index, repl.cljc)\n   226\t        │\n   227\t        ├──► Round 3 (cc3): Lowering Provenance & Oracle C1 Occurrence-Key (K) Bridge\n   228\t        │      (linearize.cljc, derive.cljc, publish.cljc:312, latte_oracle_test.clj)\n   229\t        │\n   230\t        └──► Round 4 (cc4): Four-Host Clojure C1 Replay Equality Gate & Budget Gate\n   231\t               (clojure_callsite_test.cljc across JVM + Node + Dart + Jolt)\n   232\t                        │\n   233\t                        ▼\n   234\t               Round D1: Durable Correspondence Record (:yang.correspondence/schema 1)\n   235\t                 & 7-Step Independent Reconstruction Verifier\n   236\t                 (latte_oracle_tables.clj, latte_oracle_test.clj, slice9_site_tables.edn)\n   237\t```\n   238\t\n   239\t- **Parallelism**:\n   240\t  - `cc2` (transform/REPL preservation) and `cc3` (linearize/derive provenance + oracle `K` bridge) touch disjoint functions (except a small localization in `publish.cljc`: `:312` in `publish-closure!` vs. `:487-635` in `module-from-index`) and can be developed in sequence or parallel, with `cc4` and `D1` sequenced after `cc3`.\n   241\t- **Cross-Seat Conflict Check**:\n   242\t  1. **`R3` (Exception Uniformity track, `exception-r3-impl` commit `69e7f666`)**:\n   243\t     - `69e7f666` modifies [`src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc) heavily (405 insertions, 246 deletions around try/catch/throw/outcomes lowering) and [`test/yang/clojure_test.clj`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/clojure_test.clj).\n   244\t     - **Impact**: None of `cc2`, `cc3`, `cc4`, or `D1` needs to edit `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc`! All `yang.clojure` compiler C1 hooks landed in `cc1`. Keeping `cc2`–`cc4` and `D1` out of `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` guarantees **zero merge conflict** with the exception-track seat's `R3`/`R4` work.\n   245\t  2. **`src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc` (owned by PHP/TS seat)**:\n   246\t     - Neither `cc2`–`cc4` nor `D1` touches `src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc` (Clojure uses `src/cljc/yang/clojure/prelude.cljc` and `src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc`, both already C1-annotated in `cc1`).\n   247\t\n   248\t---\n   249\t\n   250\t## 6. Owner Decisions Required Before Dispatch\n   251\t\n   252\t1. **Resolution of the Handoff vs. Design Decomposition Conflict (Section 2.1)**:\n   253\t   - Confirm that the outgoing handoff's parenthetical (*\"the three-kind correspondence: ambient literals, context-API carriers, delegation exclusion\"*) was a misattribution of the already-landed `attribution-as-query` oracle round (`d794382e`/`0f04212b`), and rule whether to execute:\n   254\t     - **Option A (Recommended)**: The 3-round Clojure pipeline completion (`cc2` transform/REPL preservation -> `cc3` lowering provenance & oracle C1 `K` bridge -> `cc4` 4-host JVM/Node/Dart/Jolt replay equality & budget gate) followed by `D1`, **or**\n   255\t     - **Option B (Compressed)**: If \"rounds 2–4\" in Design §5.3 referred only to the other three language seats (Python, TS, PHP), fold the Clojure-side oracle C1 `K` binding and 4-host equality check directly into a single pre-`D1` round + `D1`.\n   256\t2. **Runtime Trace Mechanism for `cc3` / `D1` (Design §2.5 vs. §4.2)**:\n   257\t   - Confirm whether `D1` should bind the oracle's existing caller-side site-stamped traces (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1983-2321`) to post-expansion C1 occurrence keys `K = [origin root-address path]` via verified 1-to-1 AST/linearizer provenance (preserving zero VM-step overhead on untagged runs and staying within the 4,000,000-step oracle budget), or whether the owner wants native VM frame/continuation caller-`K` propagation wired into `ast_walker`, `semantic`, `stack`, and `register` VMs before `D1`.\n   258\t3. **`slice9_site_tables.edn` Upgrade Policy in `D1`**:\n   259\t   - Confirm whether `D1` should upgrade `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn` in-place (retaining `:version 1` + integer `:site` keys alongside `:yang.correspondence/schema 1` + C1 occurrence keys `K` for additive backward compatibility, as promised in [`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3281-3283`](file:///Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj#L3281-L3283)) or emit a separate companion file `test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence.edn`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
