 The frontend's own markers named the\\n  1223\\t   pre-expansion tree; expansion, tail marking and stand-in lowering\\n  1224\\t   recompute roots and paths, so no pre-expansion table can cover this\\n  1225\\t   tree and the table is finalized here, over the finished rows. The\\n  1226\\t   origin is the run member's admission origin — the same coordinate\\n  1227\\t   the expander's event rows carry for a top-level frame. No\\n  1228\\t   expansion-record address is fabricated for the batch as a whole:\\n  1229\\t   the batch's attempts are individually recorded in the log, and the\\n  1230\\t   final tree is their admitted input's finished form.\\\"\\n  1231\\t  [row-set origin]\\n  1232\\t  (vec (sort-by pr-str\\n  1233\\t                (map (fn [[root path]] [origin root path :yang/call-site 1])\\n  1234\\t                     (vm/application-occurrences row-set)))))\\n  1235\\t\\n  1236\\t\\n  1237\\t(defn expand-batch\\n  1238\\t  \\\"Expand one input batch against `ctx` (§3.2). Returns\\n  1239\\t   `{:status :ok :tree packet :log log :ctx ctx'}` or\\n  1240\\t   `{:status :error :error e :log log :ctx ctx'}`. Either way `ctx'` has\\n  1241\\t   consumed the batch (`:t` + 1) and every attempt it allocated; only\\n  1242\\t   success changes the store, to the post-harvest store. A success also\\n  1243\\t   carries `:frontend-metadata` — the C1 side table finalized over the\\n  1244\\t   final tree (`final-call-site-metadata`), covering the tree that\\n  1245\\t   actually executes — when, and only when, the selected member itself\\n  1246\\t   claimed C1 coverage (its own verdict in `batch-call-site-claims`); a\\n  1247\\t   sibling's claim never manufactures a table for it, and an unclaimed\\n  1248\\t   batch carries no table at all, never an empty one. The table's\\n  1249\\t   occurrence origin rides beside it as `:call-site-origin`, the\\n  1250\\t   admission this expansion produced the tree under (§2.1). A context\\n  1251\\t   store binding a\\n  1252\\t   reserved name, or holding an entry without the current AST contract,\\n  1253\\t   is refused (Rule R): it is a composition defect, so it throws rather\\n  1254\\t   than returning an error.\\\"\\n  1255\\t  [batch ctx]\\n  1256\\t  (check-store! (:store ctx))\\n  1257\\t  (let [ctx (with-default-guards ctx)\\n  1258\\t        source-batch (:t ctx)\\n  1259\\t        base {:ctx ctx, :source-batch source-batch, :events [], :produced []}\\n  1260\\t        finish (fn [st]\\n  1261\\t                 (let [ctx' (update (:ctx st) :t inc)]\\n  1262\\t                   (if-let [e (:error st)]\\n  1263\\t                     {:status :error, :error e, :log (log-packet st), :ctx ctx'}\\n  1264\\t                     {:status :ok, :tree (:tree st), :log (log-packet st),\\n  1265\\t                      :frontend-metadata (:frontend-metadata st),\\n  1266\\t                      :call-site-origin (:call-site-origin st),\\n  1267\\t                      :ctx (assoc ctx' :store (:next-store st))})))\\n  1268\\t        {:keys [admitted error]} (admit batch)]\\n  1269\\t    (if error\\n  1270\\t      (let [[st counter] (allocate-attempt base)]\\n  1271\\t        (finish (-> st\\n  1272\\t                    (record-event (event-row (attempt-id ctx counter) source-batch\\n  1273\\t                                             (source-origin ctx source-batch nil)\\n  1274\\t                                             nil nil nil nil nil error))\\n  1275\\t                    (fail error))))\\n  1276\\t      (let [{:keys [trees indexes index run-index definitions]} admitted\\n  1277\\t            store0 (or (:store ctx) {})\\n  1278\\t            store (harvest store0 #(nth indexes %) definitions)\\n  1279\\t            catalogue (into []\\n  1280\\t                            (comp (filter :declared?)\\n  1281\\t                                  (map (fn [{:keys [name tree path value]}]\\n  1282\\t                                         {:name name,\\n  1283\\t          