es\n  3238\t     (mapv #(select-keys % [:id :status :recorded-deviation])\n  3239\t           (filter #(= :recorded-deviation (:status %)) results))\n  3240\t     :recorded-upstream-failures\n  3241\t     (mapv #(select-keys % [:id :status :recorded-upstream-failure])\n  3242\t           (filter #(= :recorded-upstream-failure (:status %)) results))\n  3243\t     :attribution\n  3244\t     {:version 1\n  3245\t      :rule \"caller-side site ids at compiled-AST application expressions (post-macroexpansion); records [guest-function arity caller-site]; ambient arities credit only through adapter-declared ambient-literal sites; delegations and the :gate-site/none entry site never credit\"\n  3246\t      :ambient-correspondence kernel-ambient-correspondence\n  3247\t      :site-tables-file \"slice9_site_tables.edn\"\n  3248\t      :stale-site-diagnostics\n  3249\t      (into (sorted-map)\n  3250\t            (for [row results\n  3251\t                  :let [stale (kernel-stale-sites (:site-table row)\n  3252\t                                                  {:c-walker (:c-walker row)\n  3253\t                                                   :c-semantic (:c-semantic row)})]\n  3254\t                  :when (and (seq stale) (= :pass (:status row)))]\n  3255\t              [(:id row) stale]))}\n  3256\t     :counts (frequencies (map :status results)) :fixture-count (count results)\n  3257\t     :negative-fixture-count (count (filter :negative? results))\n  3258\t     :dependency-graph\n   274\t### 5.3 Frontend-specific work packages\n   275\t\n   276\t**Clojure.** Inventory native/argument-vector/outcome compile options, `compile` vs `compile-program`, `compile-form` callers, macro expansion, `lower-unit`, `library-for`, direct walker/datoms/rows lanes, REPL single/multi-form and linked runtime publication. Show a non-oracle production fixture traversing the full pipeline, including macro-generated and helper calls. Republish `clj` and `yang.call` on each host. Oracle-specific stamping is instantiation #1 only; it does not close this brief. Anchors: `yang/clojure.cljc:2021-2034,2164-2200,2791,2839-2862,2993-3021`.\n   277\t\n   278\t**TypeScript.** Cover `lower-module-body`, `lower-unit`, `lower-units`, `lower-packet`, streaming stage, bundled and linked `js`, `yang.call`, and safepoint runtime. Track new publication/SCC/session paths from the seats when they land; do not infer their implementation from design prose. Generated member/constructor/runtime dispatch applications get their own K; source-call attribution is a separate query. Anchors: `lower.cljc:1167-1211,2262-2363`; `prelude.cljc:4168-4260`.\n   279\t\n   280\t**PHP.** Cover ANTLR and still-registered legacy compiler, include/classmap/import publication, SCC bundles/aliases, strict-types variants, prelude definition lists and P9 additions. Test by-reference/indirect calls, generators and exceptional helper paths without borrowing source-call credit. Republish `php`, dependencies and all include/import fixtures. Anchors: `php.cljc:640-685`; ANTLR `lower.cljc:1710,1812,2082,2207,3737-4041`; `publication.cljc:27-70`; `prelude_module.cljc:386`; `prelude_p9.cljc:558`.\n   281\t\n   282\t**Python.** Cover packet and module lowering, import units, SCC aliases, bundled/linked `py`, `yang.call`, `pysp`, hook staging/site-set discovery, and both fresh/primed REPL sessions. Do not conflate `:yang/site` hook sites with complete application occurrence coverage. Republish the DHT fixture and validate parserless imports on other hosts. Anchors: `lower.cljc:1111-1120,1775,2018-2373`; `repl.cljc:86-108`; `publication.cljc:51-80`; `siteset.cljc:5-31`.\n   283\t\n   284\tEach brief's acceptance bundle contains: exact producer/artifact checklist; input/commit/profile pins; C1 coverage counts and root/hash invariance; four-host results and cross-host equality report; correctness battery results; before/after budgets and measurements; legacy-load/missing-provenance refusal; and D1 verification result if it relies on correspondence. No frontend can satisfy this bundle merely by running the oracle test.\n   285\t\n   286\t## 6. Measurement and declared budgets\n   287\t\n   288\tThese are measurement requirements and design cost models, **not measured performance claims**. Signed A3 requires a budget impact per frontend, and line 29 requires static/runtime separation. This read-only design has no authority to invent benchmark results. Numeric per-corpus totals remain **unknown — the implementation round's inventory decides by measuring the pinned baseline before tagged runs**.\n   289\t\n   290\t### 6.1 Counts and cost model\n   314\t### 6.3 Bounds published before any tagged run\n   315\t\n   316\tThe implementation preflight record must contain actual finite numbers (no “TBD”, unlimited trace, or post-run adjustment) for:\n   317\t\n   318\t| Bound | Required derivation / failure |\n   319\t|---|---|\n   320\t| Maximum input rows, occurrences, A, D and total path bytes | Derive from the pinned static corpus; reject over-bound traversal before instrumentation. Include generated/bundled prelude expansion, not only source calls. |\n   321\t| Static side bytes and retained memory | Measure S without tracing; declare maximum per artifact/module and aggregate closure. Serialization size may be computed exactly before execution. Stop/revise on exceeding the declared storage/memory bound. |\n   322\t| Maximum records E and trace capacity C | Bound accepted trace writes for the fixture, declare C in records AND bytes including worst allowed site-id/path length, and declare drain behavior. No credit from a truncated/overflowed trace. |\n   323\t| Guest instruction ceiling and added work | Bound trace instructions per event/dispatch under each executed format, plus fixed setup/drain costs. Declare a ceiling for each host/format run before T; report baseline, absolute delta and ratio. |\n   324\t| Compile/expand/publish/verify/load/query time | Declare finite absolute time limits and allowed deltas against B/S in the preflight record. Pilot B/S measurements may set these; a tagged timeout is a failed bounded run. |\n   325\t| Peak process/heap/trace/index/continuation memory | Declare finite ceilings and measurement method; if a host lacks a heap counter, use a named process-memory measure and mark comparability limits. Missing measurement is not zero usage. |\n   326\t\n   327\tFor the oracle specifically, current code uses trace capacity **1,000,000 records**, drains after halt, and allows **4,000,000 guest instructions per C lane** (`latte_oracle_test.clj:1827,1847-1854,2453-2454`). These are the inspected baseline settings, not evidence the tagged run fits. Its own note records 2,024,912 walker and 1,105,792 semantic steps for the older binding fixture at line 2454. Restate both ceilings, the new record byte bound and the occupancy argument before T. If the implementation cannot establish enough capacity under those ceilings, publish revised bounds and their justification before running tagged evidence. Never silently raise fuel to get credit, or let a full trace stream park the fixture and misclassify it as semantic failure.\n   328\t\n   329\tFor other frontends, no oracle 4M/1M setting is inherited by default. Their adoption preflight must give numeric ceilings for each required fixture/prelude/host and format. Exceeding a declared bound blocks that acceptance run; changing bounds creates a new versioned run declaration and preserves the failed run.\n   330\t\n   331\t### 6.4 Budget impact allocated per frontend\n   332\t\n   333\t| Frontend | Mandatory static budget scope | Mandatory dynamic budget scope |\n   334\t|---|---|---|\n2:{:version 1, :fixtures {:beta-eq-false {:canonical-source-hash \"af0d0372c8bdc6eddb99a79c3e331c3272018c0ac689e0032f73d597b35ccd31\", :site-table {121 {:site 121, :callee gate-norm-beta-step, :arg-shapes [:computed], :def gate-norm-beta-delta-normalize, [... omitted end of long line]\n938:(defn occurrence-origin?\n967:    (when-not (occurrence-origin? origin)\n1227:  (when-not (occurrence-origin? origin)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
